WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.980
Defense contractors could see renewed interest after Lockheed Martin lands a $1.2 billion army contract for precision strike missiles. This is Modern Investing Techniques, episode 171. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always do your own research before putting real money to work.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:55.500
The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,620, down 0.5%. The NASDAQ composite closed at 26,186, down 0.6%. The TSX composite finished flat at 35,702. Oil price gains supported energy names while AI related stocks pressured broader US indices.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:15.040
19 days ago, the simulated book picked png.v on an earning surprise and it closed down 5.59%. Record short put activity of 17.75 billion dollars notional on Friday showed heavy index exposure ahead of the Wednesday Fed decision.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:32.700
Short dated put selling reached a record 17.75 billion dollars in notional exposure on Friday, with more than $11 billion tied to index puts ahead of the Fed meeting. A single $4.81 billion S&amp;P Y trade led the index portion.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:52.180
This activity reflects institutional positioning that collects premium while betting volatility will stay contained. Individual investors can mirror the approach by selling cash secured puts on broad ETFs like S&amp;P Y or XIU when the VIX sits below 20 and support levels hold.

00:01:52.180 --> 00:02:01.900
The strategy works best in low volatility regimes where the underlying trade sideways to higher but it carries assignment risk if the market gaps lower.

00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:11.740
Position sizing matters and limits exposure to 5 to 10% of portfolio cash so one adverse move does not force unwanted share ownership.

00:02:11.740 --> 00:02:29.280
Track open interest and volume on the specific strikes to gauge whether the trade is crowded. Canadian accounts using interactive brokers or quest trade can execute these trades commission-free inside a TFSA or margin account provided cash is reserved for potential assignment.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:43.220
Historical data shows the approach delivered positive expectancy in 2017 to 2019 and 2023 to 2024 when realized volatility remained below implied levels for extended periods.

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:55.300
Imagine you finished rebalancing your TFSA last quarter and now want to check whether the 6040 equity bond split still matches your targets after recent energy strength and tech weakness.

00:02:55.300 --> 00:03:03.140
Pull the actual dollar weights of each holding compare them to your stated targets and calculate the drift in percentage points.

00:03:03.760 --> 00:03:13.020
Next run a time-weighted return for the quarter using your brokerage performance report then contrast it with the money-weighted figure that accounts for any new contributions.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:27.160
Review realized gains and losses for tax-loss harvesting opportunities the for the superficial loss window closes and list every feline item to see whether MIRs or commissions exceeded 0.5% of assets.

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:42.700
Finally decide on three actions only rebalance if any asset class is more than 5% off target harvest losses on positions down more than 10% with no fundamental change or add new capital to the most underway sector.

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:57.180
The common misconception is treating the review as a simple price check. The fix is to treat it as a mechanical reconciliation of allocation, return methodology, tax position and cost structure before any new money is deployed.

00:03:57.900 --> 00:04:07.520
Investors who skip the fee audit often discover that high-cost ETFs have quietly eroded 40-60 basis points of annual return over multiple quarters.

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:19.180
A practical template starts with exporting holdings to a spreadsheet, tagging each line by asset class, then applying the 5% drift threshold before touching the buy or sell buttons.

00:04:19.940 --> 00:04:32.100
This is a simulated trade for educational purposes only. No real money is involved. This is not financial advice. The pick is Lockheed Martin on the NYSE in the industrial sector.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:46.300
The strategy is a government contract award providing near-term revenue visibility. The hold period is five sessions from entry. Invalidation occurs if the contract award is rescinded or delayed beyond the current fiscal year.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:55.540
The catalyst is a single bid 1.2 billion dollar army contract for precision strike missile increment to early operational capability.

00:04:55.540 --> 00:05:04.340
The technical setup shows price action above the 50-day moving average with volume likely to exceed the 20-day average on contract news.

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:15.220
Nearest support sits near recent swing lows. Risk assessment caps maximum acceptable loss at 8% via mental stop below the contract announcement reaction low.

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:29.680
The target is 3-6% over the five-session window if defense names attract rotation flows. Confidence sits at medium because the catalyst is confirmed but sector rotation into defense has not yet shown volume confirmation.

00:05:30.260 --> 00:05:37.480
The trade isolates a discrete verifiable catalyst and forces a rules-based exit at five sessions regardless of outcome.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:46.660
Listeners learn to size exposure to the actual capital at risk and to define invalidation before entry so the stop is never discretionary.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:55.020
The single bid language in the award notice reduces competitive uncertainty and gives a clearer revenue line item for the next two fiscal years.

00:05:55.720 --> 00:06:01.500
No newly closed trade since the last review. The most recent practice investment has already been reviewed.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:08.700
Current holdings remain open and pending their scheduled evaluation so there is no new realized result to report today.

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:16.900
The new ETF writes covered calls on aerospace and defense holdings to generate monthly income while retaining equity exposure.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:24.500
Canadian investors in taxable or registered accounts can use it to add sector beta with a built-in yield buffer during volatile periods.

00:06:24.810 --> 00:06:33.130
It trades on the TSX under the nine point high shares family and carries a management fee typical of covered call products.

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:42.970
The structure allows participants to collect option premium on names that may benefit from sustained defense spending without needing to manage individual option chains.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:51.570
Investors can access the ETF through any Canadian brokerage that supports TSX listed products including wealth simple and quest trade.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:59.990
Eldorado is hosting institutional investors at its Cassandra mines assets in Greece this week to showcase exploration progress.

00:07:00.650 --> 00:07:08.370
Analysts will visit the Scurries and Olympias projects where ongoing drilling and development work are expected to feature in updated models.

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:16.350
Add ELD.TO to the watchlist and review any post-tour notes for volume confirmation before considering entry.

00:07:16.350 --> 00:07:26.290
Savaria lifted its payout to 4.916 cents per share bringing the annual yield to 59 cents and marking the latest in a string of increases.

00:07:26.890 --> 00:07:35.570
The increase applies to dividends payable starting October 9, 2026 and qualifies as an eligible dividend under the Income Tax Act.

00:07:35.570 --> 00:07:46.570
Review SIS.TO position size in dividend focused accounts and consider adding on any post-announcement weakness if the payout ratio remains below 60%.

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:56.470
Troyless joins the GDXJ index effective September 18 as part of the quarterly rebalance bringing automatic buying from passive funds.

00:07:56.470 --> 00:08:06.110
Index funds and ETFs tracking GDXJ will adjust holdings on the rebalance state creating measurable demand that can persist for several sessions.

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:16.550
Check TLG.TO liquidity and recent volume before the rebalance state and avoid chasing if the stock has already run more than 15% into the announcement.

